[00:01.50]The cartoon depicts that a strong person is trying
[00:05.50] to dig gold out of a huge stone.
[00:08.19]Holding an ax with his firm hands,
[00:10.99]he is hewing out of the stone of despair a piece of precious gold.
[00:16.28]The caption indicates that,
[00:18.68]“Only through innovation can we make progress,
[00:22.67]while sticking to old ways means regression.” 
[00:24.67]The purpose of the drawing is to show us 
[00:29.47]that utmost importance should be attached to innovation and creativity.
[00:34.76]To begin with,
[00:35.96]the spirit of innovation could be said to 
[00:39.96]be the watchword or motto of science.
[00:42.45]Think about the innumerable times 
[00:44.45]a scientific experiment must be carried out,
[00:48.64]all the laboratory tests,
[00:50.84]all the live trials,
[00:52.54]before a new medicine or vaccine is discovered.
[00:55.73]In addition,
[00:56.83]many of today’s business successes 
[00:59.83]can be attributed to innovation.
[01:02.63]For instance,
[01:03.83]I personally worked in such a company.
[01:07.02]It was only after four years and four tries 
[01:10.02]of different business models that its entrepreneur finally succeeded,
[01:14.61]and became the chairman of one of the largest Internet companies.
[01:20.11]To sum up,
[01:21.20]in any field of endeavour,
[01:23.40]whether it be in medicine,
[01:25.60]engineering or in business,
[01:27.00]it seems necessary to put great emphasis on innovation 
[01:31.00]before one can finally achieve success.
